  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Nimish Gupta vs State Of H.P. & Others on 27 August, 2019 Bench: V. Ramasubramanian, Anoop Chitkara In The High Court Of Himachal Pradesh, Shimla Cwp No.1155 of 2017 . Decided on: 27.08.2019 Nimish Gupta ...Petitioner Versus State of H.P. & others ..Respondents Coram The Hon'ble Mr. Justice V. Ramasubramanian, Chief Justice The Hon'ble Mr. Justice Anoop Chitkara, Judge",
    "facts": "The petitioner has come up with the above writ petition seeking a writ of mandamus to direct the respondents to take immediate steps (i) for the implementation of the provisions of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006; (ii) for the setting up of the Food Authority as per the mandate of the Act; and (iii) for the appointment of special prosecutors for prosecuting the persons who are guilty of the offences under the Act. Subsequently, certain directions were issued for filing affidavits and the status reports. \" This case has engaged the attention of this Court re: implementation of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 in the State of Himachal Pradesh. A fresh Status Report was asked for vide order dated 7.3.2019 and pursuant thereto, the Director, Health Safety and Regulations, Himachal Pradesh has filed Report dated 29.4.2019. It is explained that 19 posts of Food Safety Officers were advertised by the Himachal Pradesh Staff Selection Commission and 54 candidates applied in response thereto, but all were declared ineligible. Hence, no selection was made. Some of those candidates approached the Himachal Pradesh Administrative Tribunal and learned Additional Advocate General informs that vide order dated 18.3.2019, the Tribunal has accepted . their claim declaring them eligible. Directions have been issued to reconsider them within two months.",
    "arguments": "Nimish Gupta vs State Of H.P. & Others on 27 August, 2019 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/37905775/ 3 7.",
